# Repo And Clips Workflow

This workflow combines repository browsing surfaces and clip-sharing surfaces.

## 1. Navigate repository browser in web UI

Primary route family:

- `/repos/:owner/:repo`
- `/repos/:owner/:repo/tree/:path`
- `/repos/:owner/:repo/blob/:path`
- `/repos/:owner/:repo/blame/:path`
- `/repos/:owner/:repo/commit/:sha`
- `/repos/:owner/:repo/compare/:refs`

These pages are backed by server routes under `/api/repos/{owner}/{name}/*`.

## 2. Use Git smart protocol endpoints when needed

Server routes include:

- `/git/{owner}/{repo}/info/refs`
- `/git/{owner}/{repo}/git-upload-pack`
- `/git/{owner}/{repo}/git-receive-pack`

Clips also expose Git-style endpoints under `/git/clips/{owner}/{name}/*`.

## 3. Create and iterate clips

Web clip routes:

- `/clips/new`
- `/clips/:owner/:name`
- `/clips/:owner/:name/edit`
- `/clips/:owner/:name/revisions`

API routes include create/fork/update/delete/list/star operations under `/api/clips/*`.

## 4. Coordinate Loom thread context with repo work

When using CLI for implementation assistance:

```bash
loom
loom search "repo migration decision"
```

Capture key commit references in thread prompts so later search and handoff are reliable.

<Callout variant="tip" title="Clip publication pattern">
	Use clips for concise, reviewable snippets while keeping long-form implementation rationale in Loom threads.
</Callout>
